      "hints": [
        "Surface area $S = 2(2x^2 + 4x^2 + 8x^2) = 28x^2$ and Volume $V = 8x^3$.",
        "Show $7V^{2/3} = 7(8x^3)^{2/3} = 7(4x^2) = 28x^2 = S$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express the surface area $S$ and volume $V$ in terms of $x$:\n$$S = 2(x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot 4x + 2x \\cdot 4x) = 2(2x^2 + 4x^2 + 8x^2) = 2(14x^2) = 28x^2$$\n$$V = x \\cdot 2x \\cdot 4x = 8x^3$$",
        "Evaluate $7V^{2/3}$:\n$$7V^{2/3} = 7(8x^3)^{2/3} = 7(8^{2/3})(x^3)^{2/3} = 7(4)(x^2) = 28x^2$$",
        "Conclude that $S = 7V^{2/3}$."
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Surface Area and Volume Relations": "Finds $S = 28x^2$ and $V = 8x^3$ (B2). Shows $7V^{2/3} = S$ (B1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
      }
