      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $S = 7V^{2/3}$ to get $\\frac{dS}{dV} = \\frac{14}{3}V^{-1/3}$.",
        "At $V = 1000$, $\\frac{dS}{dV} = \\frac{14}{30} = \\frac{7}{15}$, then $\\frac{dV}{dt} = \\frac{dS/dt}{dS/dV} = \\frac{2}{7/15} = \\frac{30}{7}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $S = 7V^{2/3}$ with respect to $V$:\n$$\\frac{dS}{dV} = 7\\left(\\frac{2}{3}V^{-1/3}\\right) = \\frac{14}{3}V^{-1/3}$$",
        "Evaluate $\\frac{dS}{dV}$ at $V = 1000\\text{ cm}^3$:\n$$\\left.\\frac{dS}{dV}\\right|_{V=1000} = \\frac{14}{3}(1000^{-1/3}) = \\frac{14}{3(10)} = \\frac{14}{30} = \\frac{7}{15}$$",
        "Apply the chain rule for connected rates of change with $\\frac{dS}{dt} = 2\\text{ cm}^2/\\text{s}$:\n$$\\frac{dV}{dt} = \\frac{dS/dt}{dS/dV} = \\frac{2}{\\frac{7}{15}} = 2 \\times \\frac{15}{7} = \\frac{30}{7}\\text{ cm}^3\\text{ s}^{-1} \\quad (\\approx 4.29\\text{ cm}^3\\text{ s}^{-1})$$"
      ],
